## COPY THIS FILE INTO THE PARENT DIRECTORY ##
###  Inputs  :---------------- 
Line-1:         norb,nlctrns,amltplt
Line-2:         accu,nbonds,vrp
Line-3:         (trnsfr(i),i=1,nbonds)
Line-4:        (ibond(1,i),ibond(2,i),i=1,nbonds)
Line-5:        (uhub(i),i=1,norb)
Line-6:         (esite(i),i=1,norb)
Line-7:         (nzocc(i),i=1,norb)
Line-8:         (vatt(i),i=1,norb-1)
Line-9:         (amg(i),i=1,norb)


norb: number of orbitals (or number of sites)
nlctrns: number of electrons
amltplt: total spin multiplicity (for spin conserved) calculation
accu: accuracy
nbonds: number of bonds
vrp: dipole interaction strength
trnsfr: hopping strength (also termed as transfer or overlap integral)
ibond:  the 'bonds', i.e. the pairs of site indices between  which the hopping occurs
ubub(i): hubbard interaction strength for each site i
esite: on-site energy or chemical potential
nzocc(=1) : integer filling used in case the V-term is written as Σ V_ij(n_i - 1)(n_j - 1)[[NOT USED IN CODE]]
vatt: nearest neighbour Coulomb interaction  in case of Extended Hubbard Model
amg: magnetic field strength interacting with Sz (z-component of spin)
